WEBVTT

00:01.940 --> 00:11.820
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:02.580 --> 00:05.020
All right, everyone! Let us put some spirit into this!

00:06.650 --> 00:07.900
My bro is so weird...

00:08.680 --> 00:10.690
Usually he'd be wheezing from exhaustion by now.

00:11.170 --> 00:12.930
He really must be looking forward to it, huh?

00:13.130 --> 00:13.740
Of course!

00:14.410 --> 00:16.120
It is the festival centered around Electric Pokémon,

00:16.620 --> 00:18.270
the Thunder Festival!

00:19.060 --> 00:23.460
As an Electric Pokémon user, I have always wanted to go there one day.

00:24.380 --> 00:26.960
In ancient times, a large thunderbolt Thunder sent down...

00:27.570 --> 00:30.010
...split a large tree in a town right in two.

00:30.700 --> 00:34.280
However, mysteriously, that tree grew healthier and taller than ever,

00:34.600 --> 00:36.770
and carried many fruit.

00:37.500 --> 00:45.040
Delighted, the townspeople started the Thunder Festival in the hopes that Thunder would once again appear and make the town more fertile.

00:45.390 --> 00:45.970
The end.

00:46.860 --> 00:47.800
What's "Thunder"?

00:48.590 --> 00:50.830
It is a Pokémon that freely controls lightning bolts.

00:52.610 --> 00:55.500
Fire, the Flame Pokémon we saw together with Trova back then,

00:56.540 --> 00:58.280
the Freeze Pokémon Freezer,

00:59.440 --> 01:00.580
and Thunder:

01:01.660 --> 01:06.220
these three together are called the three legendary great bird Pokémon.

01:07.160 --> 01:09.680
Wow, a legendary Pokémon?

01:09.880 --> 01:11.870
Eureka wants to see it too!

01:18.590 --> 01:19.460
Thunder?!

01:20.260 --> 01:20.800
Is that the one?

01:21.260 --> 01:22.260
I've never seen Thunder before.

01:22.770 --> 01:24.930
So it is already close by.

01:28.090 --> 01:29.800
I saw it, I saw it!

01:30.360 --> 01:31.380
It's so cool, right?

01:31.380 --> 01:31.870
Yeah!

01:33.600 --> 01:36.290
There is no time to idle. Let us hurry ahead!

01:36.920 --> 01:38.900
Uh, hey... Don't rush, Citron!

01:39.780 --> 01:44.700
If we are not in town by the time Thunder visits the festival, we will miss the main event!

01:55.390 --> 01:56.840
Citron, are you all right?

01:57.490 --> 01:59.930
Th-That was a close call.

02:06.820 --> 02:08.420
It looks somewhat angry.

02:08.930 --> 02:09.950
I wonder what the matter is.

02:15.630 --> 02:17.380
Right now, the road to the town will be dangerous.

02:18.210 --> 02:20.160
Isn't there any place where we could take shelter...?

02:21.360 --> 02:22.330
There is a cave!

02:23.130 --> 02:25.200
All right! Let's go there for now.

02:29.240 --> 02:34.910
Thunder and Onvern!
A Furious Strike of Lightning!!

02:35.940 --> 02:39.360
As Satoshi and his friends make their way through a forest on their way to the Thunder Festival,

02:35.950 --> 02:45.840
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

02:35.950 --> 02:45.840
Z

02:39.700 --> 02:44.560
they encounter Thunder and escape into a cave to avoid its lightning.

02:46.390 --> 02:48.380
Wow, that was scary!

02:48.930 --> 02:51.400
As long as we stay here, we should be fine for now.

02:52.210 --> 02:56.480
I wonder if we will make it to Ikazuchi Town before the Thunder Festival begins.

02:57.180 --> 02:59.230
Ikazuchi Town, you say?

03:05.970 --> 03:08.020
Wait, wait! Calm down for a second!

03:09.260 --> 03:10.500
I'm sorry for startling you.

03:11.310 --> 03:12.130
I'm Stan.

03:12.770 --> 03:14.250
I'm a rescue worker.

03:15.320 --> 03:16.320
Your leg...

03:16.670 --> 03:17.210
Yeah.

03:17.880 --> 03:20.160
I went for wool and ended up getting shorn.

03:21.180 --> 03:24.560
A lightning bolt caused me to lose control over my car.

03:38.360 --> 03:40.320
Uhm... Are you all right?

03:41.080 --> 03:41.590
Yeah.

03:42.210 --> 03:43.560
I performed some first aid.

03:44.280 --> 03:47.070
More importantly, I have a favor to ask you.

03:47.640 --> 03:48.600
A favor?

03:49.200 --> 03:53.280
The thing is, I want you to deliver this to the town's hospital.

03:54.430 --> 03:56.210
There are children there waiting for it.

03:56.640 --> 04:00.180
I want to deliver it quickly, but unfortunately, in this state...

04:01.250 --> 04:03.650
I'm terribly sorry to make such an unreasonable request.

04:04.300 --> 04:05.910
Please... will you do this for me?

04:07.200 --> 04:08.680
We just need to deliver this, right?

04:09.480 --> 04:10.200
Can I count on you?

04:11.540 --> 04:12.320
Of course.

04:16.140 --> 04:18.950
But what can we do in this lightningstorm?

04:19.430 --> 04:22.590
This cave used to be connected to the town as well,

04:23.270 --> 04:25.700
but nowadays you've got to take the outside routes.

04:26.940 --> 04:29.560
A rockfall blocked it a long time ago, see.

04:31.180 --> 04:33.190
The route has gone unused ever since.

04:33.650 --> 04:34.440
Don't worry.

04:34.860 --> 04:35.860
Now that we know this...

04:37.280 --> 04:38.880
Luchabull, I choose you!

04:42.120 --> 04:44.790
Luchabull, use Karate Chop to smash that rock!

04:52.830 --> 04:54.080
Good job, Luchabull!

04:57.800 --> 04:58.950
All right, next...

05:00.200 --> 05:01.700
Onbat, I choose you!

05:05.280 --> 05:09.380
Use Supersonic to find the shortest route to the exit and guide us there!

05:10.960 --> 05:12.070
Tairenar, please!

05:15.180 --> 05:17.000
Can you use your flame to light up the surroundings?

05:20.480 --> 05:21.460
All right, we're off.

05:22.260 --> 05:24.710
Once we arrive in the city, we will ask someone to come help you.

05:25.170 --> 05:25.580
Okay.

05:26.140 --> 05:26.940
Thanks.

05:39.810 --> 05:41.370
Onbat, I'm counting on you!

05:53.960 --> 05:55.380
All right, everyone. Let's go!

06:13.280 --> 06:14.960
What are you gonna do, Nyarth?!

06:14.960 --> 06:16.390
Thunder is furious!

06:16.580 --> 06:20.900
According to my plan, we were supposed to be able to catch it more easily now...

06:21.110 --> 06:22.510
Whoa! It's coming back!

06:24.860 --> 06:27.480
In this case, the best defense is a good offense!

06:27.960 --> 06:29.990
Fire electromagnetic fields repeatedly! Repeatedly!

06:30.400 --> 06:31.600
Understood!

06:39.010 --> 06:40.260
What?!

06:47.280 --> 06:47.900
Dodge!

06:48.580 --> 06:49.910
Dodging!

06:55.420 --> 06:56.920
They don't call it "legendary" for nothing...

07:08.600 --> 07:09.350
Onbat!

07:13.860 --> 07:15.030
Ow...

07:15.030 --> 07:16.470
Is everyone all right?

07:17.120 --> 07:17.530
Satoshi!

07:18.750 --> 07:20.530
Satoshi! Onbat! Luchabull!

07:21.430 --> 07:22.480
We're all fine here.

07:24.140 --> 07:24.770
How about you guys?

07:25.950 --> 07:27.860
Everyone is safe, Satoshi!

07:28.870 --> 07:29.700
Thank goodness...

07:32.130 --> 07:33.460
Calm down, Onbat.

07:34.840 --> 07:36.470
We're here.

07:42.860 --> 07:44.280
We'll get rid of these rocks now.

07:48.870 --> 07:50.100
Wait, Luchabull!

07:50.350 --> 07:51.410
It looks like it's going to collapse!

07:53.710 --> 07:54.230
Satoshi,

07:54.840 --> 07:58.150
we're going to try heading to the city together with Stan-san.

07:58.770 --> 08:01.010
You guys go on ahead without us!

08:01.010 --> 08:03.670
Please deliver the medicine as soon as possible!

08:03.670 --> 08:05.080
They're waiting for the medicine!

08:05.670 --> 08:07.340
You're right. I got it!

08:08.900 --> 08:11.780
Serena, you and the others be careful too! I'm counting on you!

08:12.240 --> 08:12.620
Yeah!

08:15.180 --> 08:15.650
Let's go!

08:26.690 --> 08:27.780
Pokémon Quiz.

08:28.370 --> 08:29.140
The answer is...?

08:47.900 --> 08:48.600
Again, huh...

08:49.800 --> 08:50.530
Onbat!

08:58.920 --> 09:00.060
Which way is it, Onbat?

09:13.550 --> 09:14.000
That way.

09:14.360 --> 09:14.780
Let's hurry!

09:24.320 --> 09:25.660
You did it, Onbat!

09:49.780 --> 09:50.340
Whoa!

09:52.770 --> 09:53.480
Thunder?!

09:53.910 --> 09:54.850
What is it doing here...?

09:58.600 --> 09:59.350
Who is it?

10:01.620 --> 10:04.130
If you ask "Who is it? Pika?",

10:04.980 --> 10:07.320
It is the world's mercy that makes us answer.

10:08.160 --> 10:10.830
To prevent the world's destruction.

10:11.630 --> 10:14.830
To protect the world's peace.

10:15.840 --> 10:18.480
Carrying out the evil of love and truth,

10:18.740 --> 10:21.550
we're lovely, charmy villains.

10:22.300 --> 10:22.820
Musashi!

10:23.340 --> 10:24.050
Kojiro!

10:24.670 --> 10:27.390
For the Rocket Gang duo dashing across the galaxy,

10:28.060 --> 10:30.780
a white hole, a white tomorrow awaits ahead!

10:31.590 --> 10:33.310
Just kidding!

10:34.020 --> 10:34.910
Rocket Gang!

10:36.760 --> 10:38.810
Geez, Thunder! You're pesky!

10:39.310 --> 10:40.660
Give it a rest already!

10:40.660 --> 10:41.990
I'm sick of this!

10:44.120 --> 10:44.650
Nyarth?!

10:45.480 --> 10:47.350
Ow...

10:49.310 --> 10:50.950
What's this about, guys?

10:51.940 --> 10:53.910
You've been up to no good again, haven't you?

10:54.960 --> 10:56.400
You're wrong!

10:57.060 --> 11:02.390
As always, we were trying to boldly capture a Pokémon.

11:08.180 --> 11:12.030
But we messed up a little and then Thunder happened...

11:13.800 --> 11:15.330
I see.

11:16.270 --> 11:18.440
So that's why Thunder is angry.

11:20.110 --> 11:21.940
I told you, you lose your head too easily...

11:23.340 --> 11:25.190
Let's ask Thunder to let us pass.

11:26.230 --> 11:27.160
What?!

11:27.600 --> 11:29.150
I've got to deliver some medicine.

11:29.730 --> 11:32.340
What are you talking about? If you go out there now...

11:32.340 --> 11:33.300
It will understand if we explain the situation!

11:35.000 --> 11:37.400
Also, this is all your fault to begin with!

11:38.660 --> 11:39.440
Let's go, everyone!

11:41.880 --> 11:44.520
It's in times like this we need to work together with him!

11:44.520 --> 11:47.090
That's right. If we get separated from him, Thunder will just go after <i>us</i>.

11:47.280 --> 11:50.470
Hey, wait! I'm coming too!

11:51.460 --> 11:53.160
You'll only make things confusing, stay away!

11:57.150 --> 11:57.790
Thunder!

11:58.050 --> 11:59.170
We're not your enemies!

11:59.490 --> 12:00.470
Please let us go!

12:09.590 --> 12:12.860
Please calm down! Let's go to the Thunder Festival together!

12:15.560 --> 12:16.220
It's no use...

12:17.570 --> 12:19.820
In that case, we have no choice but to go for it.

12:20.280 --> 12:21.710
Fiarrow, I choose you!

12:24.460 --> 12:26.380
Please, attract Thunder's attention!

12:39.590 --> 12:40.820
I'm counting on you, Fiarrow.

13:20.190 --> 13:21.100
Return, Fiarrow!

13:33.260 --> 13:35.560
Onbat, let's leave this to Luchabull.

13:35.990 --> 13:36.440
Let's go!

13:56.240 --> 13:56.680
Onbat!

14:10.200 --> 14:10.710
Onbat!

14:39.440 --> 14:41.110
It... evolved.

14:45.120 --> 14:46.980
Onvern, the Sound Wave Pokémon.

14:47.580 --> 14:51.470
The ultrasonic waves it blasts from its ears can even crush rocks.

14:55.260 --> 14:56.770
Luchabull, well done.

14:59.250 --> 14:59.980
Onvern...

15:23.140 --> 15:23.700
That's...

15:26.880 --> 15:27.590
I see.

15:28.160 --> 15:30.110
Onvern has learned Boomburst, huh?

15:41.800 --> 15:42.290
That's right.

15:43.030 --> 15:48.680
Make use of this terrain! Use your Supersonic to outsmart your opponent while hiding among the rocks!

16:10.610 --> 16:11.860
Now, use Boomburst!

16:23.800 --> 16:26.990
Now that the brat boy's Onvern is attracting its attention...

16:27.700 --> 16:29.870
...we just <i>have</i> to get Thunder!

16:30.450 --> 16:32.860
Electromagnetic Capture Missile, fire!

16:41.550 --> 16:43.030
We did it!

16:43.280 --> 16:45.600
We caught it, we caught it!

16:46.260 --> 16:47.310
Rocket Gang!

16:48.230 --> 16:50.370
Thunder is ours now!

16:51.040 --> 16:53.160
We got you good there!

16:53.790 --> 16:57.320
You guys should hurry up and deliver the medicine!

16:57.980 --> 16:59.020
You guys...

17:03.750 --> 17:05.700
Onvern, let's save Thunder!

17:08.820 --> 17:10.110
Ugh, what's going on?

17:10.550 --> 17:12.670
After an opportunity comes big trouble!

17:13.250 --> 17:14.770
Onvern, Boomburst!

17:15.240 --> 17:16.910
Pikachu, you use Thunderbolt!

17:26.150 --> 17:28.400
This feels bad!

17:32.220 --> 17:35.440
Onvern, use Acrobatics to cut Thunder's rope!

17:50.470 --> 17:51.440
Thunder!

17:51.950 --> 17:53.330
So it understands now.

18:01.200 --> 18:03.150
Thank you, Thunder!

18:09.870 --> 18:11.270
You did well, Onvern.

18:16.850 --> 18:18.540
All right, let's hurry!

18:28.770 --> 18:30.160
You really were of great help.

18:30.660 --> 18:33.240
It was nothing. I hope they'll get better soon.

18:33.700 --> 18:34.230
Goodbye.

18:34.940 --> 18:35.920
Thank you very much.

18:37.350 --> 18:40.520
All right, Pikachu. Let's go look for Serena and the others.

18:42.320 --> 18:43.490
Satoshi!

18:45.360 --> 18:45.970
What about the medicine?

18:46.540 --> 18:47.890
We managed to deliver it just fine.

18:48.510 --> 18:49.470
That's great!

18:50.360 --> 18:51.040
What about Stan-san?

18:51.890 --> 18:53.480
He's fine, of course.

18:54.220 --> 18:56.320
He is getting treated by Joy-san right now.

18:56.930 --> 18:58.690
It appears it was nothing serious.

18:59.140 --> 18:59.750
I see.

19:02.220 --> 19:03.690
Oh, right. Look.

19:10.830 --> 19:11.720
An Onvern?

19:12.120 --> 19:13.410
Could Onbat possibly...

19:13.800 --> 19:14.910
...have evolved...?

19:15.400 --> 19:15.810
Yeah.

19:16.270 --> 19:18.660
I wish I could've seen it evolve.

19:21.090 --> 19:23.260
That guy did a brilliant job.

19:45.940 --> 19:47.340
Look, it's Thunder!

19:47.880 --> 19:50.160
The Thunder Festival has begun.

19:50.690 --> 19:52.460
All right, let's have fun!

19:52.680 --> 19:53.780
I have been waiting for this!

19:53.780 --> 19:54.660
So has Eureka!

19:59.520 --> 20:05.030
Having saved the legendary Pokémon Thunder, Satoshi and his friends managed to attend the Thunder Festival.

20:05.960 --> 20:11.180
With Onbat having evolved into Onvern, their journey once again is...

20:15.880 --> 20:20.840
Sunday March 6th at 8am!

20:16.470 --> 20:20.060
Poké it out, yo, Bald it out, yo! Poké it out, yo, Bald it out, yo!

20:17.330 --> 20:20.060
The Baldket Gang has come to hijack Pokénchi!

20:20.880 --> 20:24.860
Professor Okido

20:20.890 --> 20:24.860
Pokémon movie news!

20:21.040 --> 20:22.300
Pokémon movie news!

20:22.690 --> 20:24.390
Here is the latest footage!

20:25.690 --> 20:27.780
Based on the creations of
Satoshi Tajiri

20:27.900 --> 20:30.030
Directed by
Kunihiko Yuyama

20:28.210 --> 20:29.830
Ya can't trust humans.

20:30.220 --> 20:32.490
The Soul Heart is mine!

20:34.610 --> 20:36.690
What is Volcanion's true motive?

20:37.360 --> 20:37.980
And...

20:38.120 --> 20:39.830
The Soul Heart

20:39.830 --> 20:41.020
I'll go too!

20:41.120 --> 20:42.460
What is its secret?

20:43.200 --> 20:46.630
A Pokémon nobody knows of finally shows itself!

20:47.560 --> 20:49.920
Pokémon the movie XY&Z:

20:50.370 --> 20:52.800
Volcanion and the Ingenious Magearna

20:53.010 --> 20:54.890
Premieres Saturday July 16th!

20:55.650 --> 20:58.180
Magearna, a Pokémon created by humans...

21:00.280 --> 21:02.450
...and Volcanion, who hates humans.

21:02.770 --> 21:03.880
Get blown away!

21:05.230 --> 21:08.680
Magearna and Volcanion... Are they enemies or allies?

21:09.520 --> 21:12.060
Also, what is Magearna's unknown power?

21:12.860 --> 21:15.160
For more info, check out the homepage!

21:18.080 --> 21:19.970
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:20.160 --> 21:21.220
Towards our next adventure!

21:22.260 --> 21:23.150
Notice:

21:24.080 --> 21:31.170
Tonight, I will visit the exhibit of the world's jewels in the Jackal Town Hotel to take the hardest object in the world.

